#: src/configuring-languages.md:74
msgid "Working with Language Servers"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:76
msgid ""
"Language servers are a crucial part of Zed's intelligent coding features, "
"providing capabilities like auto-completion, go-to-definition, and real-time "
"error checking."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:78
msgid "What are Language Servers?"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:80
msgid ""
"Language servers implement the Language Server Protocol (LSP), which "
"standardizes communication between the editor and language-specific tools. "
"This allows Zed to support advanced features for multiple programming "
"languages without implementing each feature separately."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:82
msgid "Some key features provided by language servers include:"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:84
msgid "Code completion"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:85
msgid "Error checking and diagnostics"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:86
msgid "Code navigation (go to definition, find references)"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:87
msgid "Code actions (Rename, extract method)"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:88
msgid "Hover information"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:89
msgid "Workspace symbol search"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:91
msgid "Managing Language Servers"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:93
msgid "Zed simplifies language server management for users:"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:95
msgid ""
"Automatic Download: When you open a file with a matching file type, Zed "
"automatically downloads the appropriate language server. Zed may prompt you "
"to install an extension for known file types."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:97
msgid "Storage Location:"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:99
msgid "macOS: `~/Library/Application Support/Zed/languages`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:100
msgid ""
"Linux: `$XDG_DATA_HOME/zed/languages`, `$FLATPAK_XDG_DATA_HOME/zed/"
"languages`, or `$HOME/.local/share/zed/languages`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:102
msgid ""
"Automatic Updates: Zed keeps your language servers up-to-date, ensuring you "
"always have the latest features and improvements."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:104
msgid "Choosing Language Servers"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:106
msgid ""
"Some languages in Zed offer multiple language server options. You might have "
"multiple extensions installed that bundle language servers targeting the "
"same language, potentially leading to overlapping capabilities. To ensure "
"you get the functionality you prefer, Zed allows you to prioritize which "
"language servers are used and in what order."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:108
msgid "You can specify your preference using the `language_servers` setting:"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:112
msgid "\"PHP\""
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:113
msgid "\"language_servers\""
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:113
msgid "\"intelephense\""
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:113
msgid "\"!phpactor\""
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:113
msgid "\"!phptools\""
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:113
msgid "\"...\""
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:118
msgid "In this example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:120
msgid "`intelephense` is set as the primary language server"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:121
msgid "`phpactor` is disabled (note the `!` prefix)"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:122
msgid ""
"`...` expands to the rest of the language servers that are registered for PHP"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:124
msgid ""
"This configuration allows you to tailor the language server setup to your "
"specific needs, ensuring that you get the most suitable functionality for "
"your development workflow."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:126
msgid "Toolchains"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-languages.md:128
msgid ""
"Some language servers need to be configured with a current \"toolchain\", "
"which is an installation of a specific version of a programming language "
"compiler or/and interpreter, which can possibly include a full set of "
"dependencies of a project. An example of what Zed considers a toolchain is a "
"virtual environment in Python. Not all languages in Zed support toolchain "
"discovery and selection, but for those that do, you can specify the "
"toolchain from a toolchain picker (via <code class=\"hljs\">toolchain: "
"select</code>). To learn more about toolchains in Zed, see [`toolchains`](./"
"toolchains.md)."
msgstr ""

